{
  "version": 1,
  "description": [
    "The workspace contract, asserted by three independent drivers: the Go runner",
    "against the CLI, the TypeScript wrapper, and the Python wrapper. Every driver",
    "reads this one file, so a client cannot disagree with the engine about what a",
    "verb returns without one of them failing.",
    "",
    "This exists because the client wrappers had never been run against the binary",
    "they wrap. They were wrong in the same way in both languages: `handoff",
    "--output` writes the document to the named path and prints nothing, and both",
    "decoded stdout anyway. The divergence that hid it is what kept the surface out",
    "of CI. The 'handoff' step below is that regression, stated once.",
    "",
    "Absolute paths, workspace ids, checkpoint ids and digests are generated per",
    "run, so no step states one literally. The harness owns the work directory,",
    "isolates the default registry under a temporary home, substitutes",
    "{{captures}} into arguments, and applies a step's 'write' block so a step can",
    "change the workspace the way an agent would.",
    "",
    "A team's partition is a directory boundary, not a label: a checkpoint filed",
    "under teams/<name> is invisible from the registry root, so a delta across two",
    "teams cannot even be attempted \u2014 the checkpoint is simply not found. The",
    "'crosses workspaces' refusal is therefore reachable only between two",
    "workspaces inside one partition, which is what the scenario does. Both",
    "boundaries are real; only one of them is a refusal with a message.",
    "",
    "A handoff reference names a workspace; it does not transfer its identity.",
    "resume --handoff therefore returns the workspace the document names, in the",
    "registry the document recorded, while adopt builds a different workspace from",
    "the archive. Both are asserted, because a caller that assumed the two returned",
    "the same id would resume the sender's workspace instead of the receiver's.",
    "",
    "resume takes the registry from the document and refuses --handoff alongside",
    "--registry-dir. A caller that could point a handoff at a different registry",
    "would resume a workspace in a place the document never named, so the refusal",
    "is a safety property and is asserted rather than worked around.",
    "",
    "The substitution step is the one worth reading twice. A delta's own digests",
    "cover its content bytes and nothing else, so renaming an addition in the",
    "change list and in the content map together leaves the document entirely",
    "self-consistent: the content digest still matches, and the precondition passes",
    "because the new name is absent from the base. Applied without a digest it",
    "produces a published checkpoint holding a file the sender never named. The",
    "check that stops it is the one the handoff archive path already had, applied",
    "to the delta path where it was missing."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "prepare seeds every declared input and reports the totals it seeded",
      "verb": "prepare",
      "registry": "a",
      "manifest": {
        "root": "{{work}}/workspace",
        "team": "platform",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "body": "seed",
            "destination": "seed.txt"
          },
          {
            "body": "second",
            "destination": "nested/second.txt"
          }
        ]
      },
      "capture": {
        "ws": "workspace_id",
        "root": "root",
        "registryA": "registry_dir"
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspace_id": {
          "matches": "^ws_[0-9a-f]+$"
        },
        "seeded_objects": {
          "equals": 2
        },
        "seeded_bytes": {
          "equals": 10
        },
        "team": {
          "equals": "platform"
        },
        "root": {
          "equals": "{{work}}/workspace"
        },
        "registry_dir": {
          "underWork": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the seeded inputs are really on disk, at the destinations the manifest named",
      "verb": "read",
      "root": "{{work}}/workspace",
      "expect": {
        "seed.txt": {
          "equals": "seed"
        },
        "nested/second.txt": {
          "equals": "second"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "checkpoint counts the same files and bytes the seed did",
      "verb": "checkpoint",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "id": "{{ws}}"
      },
      "capture": {
        "cp1": "checkpoint_id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "matches": "^cp_[0-9a-f]+$"
        },
        "workspace_id": {
          "equals": "{{ws}}"
        },
        "files": {
          "equals": 2
        },
        "bytes": {
          "equals": 10
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "an agent changes the workspace between checkpoints",
      "verb": "noop",
      "write": [
        {
          "path": "notes.txt",
          "body": "written by the agent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a second checkpoint names the first as its parent and counts the new file",
      "verb": "checkpoint",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "id": "{{ws}}",
        "parent": "{{cp1}}"
      },
      "capture": {
        "cp2": "checkpoint_id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "parent_checkpoint_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp1}}"
        },
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "notEquals": "{{cp1}}"
        },
        "files": {
          "equals": 3
        },
        "bytes": {
          "equals": 30
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "diff between the two checkpoints names only what the agent changed",
      "verb": "diff",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "from": "{{cp1}}",
        "to": "{{cp2}}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "changes": {
          "length": 1
        },
        "changes[0].path": {
          "equals": "notes.txt"
        },
        "changes[0].kind": {
          "equals": "added"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a second workspace can share the registry without sharing the workspace",
      "verb": "prepare",
      "registry": "a",
      "manifest": {
        "root": "{{work}}/workspace2",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "body": "elsewhere",
            "destination": "other.txt"
          }
        ],
        "team": "platform"
      },
      "capture": {
        "ws2": "workspace_id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspace_id": {
          "notEquals": "{{ws}}"
        },
        "seeded_objects": {
          "equals": 1
        },
        "root": {
          "equals": "{{work}}/workspace2"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a checkpoint of the second workspace is its own, in the same registry",
      "verb": "checkpoint",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "id": "{{ws2}}"
      },
      "capture": {
        "cpB": "checkpoint_id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspace_id": {
          "equals": "{{ws2}}"
        },
        "files": {
          "equals": 1
        },
        "bytes": {
          "equals": 9
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a delta across two workspaces is refused, which is why this is not version control",
      "verb": "delta",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "from": "{{cp1}}",
        "to": "{{cpB}}",
        "output": "{{work}}/crossed.stowdelta"
      },
      "fail": {
        "contains": "crosses workspaces"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "handoff without an archive is a local reference, version 1",
      "verb": "handoff",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "id": "{{ws}}",
        "output": "{{work}}/local-handoff.json"
      },
      "alsoWritten": "local-handoff.json",
      "expect": {
        "version": {
          "equals": 1
        },
        "workspace_id": {
          "equals": "{{ws}}"
        },
        "team": {
          "equals": "platform"
        },
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "absent": true
        }
      },
      "returns": "file"
    },
    {
      "id": "handoff with an archive is a portable reference, version 2",
      "verb": "handoff",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "id": "{{ws}}",
        "checkpoint-id": "{{cp2}}",
        "archive": "{{work}}/checkpoint.tar.gz",
        "output": "{{work}}/handoff.json"
      },
      "alsoWritten": "handoff.json",
      "expect": {
        "version": {
          "equals": 2
        },
        "workspace_id": {
          "equals": "{{ws}}"
        },
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp2}}"
        },
        "team": {
          "equals": "platform"
        },
        "archive.path": {
          "equals": "{{work}}/checkpoint.tar.gz"
        },
        "archive.sha256": {
          "matches": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
        },
        "archive.files": {
          "equals": 3
        },
        "archive.bytes": {
          "min": 1
        }
      },
      "returns": "file"
    },
    {
      "id": "adopt restores the archive into a registry that has never seen it",
      "verb": "adopt",
      "registry": "default",
      "args": {
        "handoff": "{{work}}/handoff.json",
        "root": "{{work}}/adopted"
      },
      "capture": {
        "adopted": "workspace_id"
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspace_id": {
          "notEquals": "{{ws}}"
        },
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp2}}"
        },
        "team": {
          "equals": "platform"
        },
        "root": {
          "equals": "{{work}}/adopted"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the adopted workspace holds the agent's file, not only the seed",
      "verb": "read",
      "root": "{{work}}/adopted",
      "expect": {
        "notes.txt": {
          "equals": "written by the agent"
        },
        "nested/second.txt": {
          "equals": "second"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "resume takes the registry from the document, not from a flag",
      "verb": "resume",
      "args": {
        "handoff": "{{work}}/handoff.json"
      },
      "expect": {
        "workspace_id": {
          "equals": "{{ws}}"
        },
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp2}}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "resume refuses to override the registry a handoff document names",
      "verb": "resume",
      "registry": "a",
      "args": {
        "handoff": "{{work}}/handoff.json"
      },
      "fail": {
        "contains": "not both"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "delta names both ends, and writes the document it describes",
      "verb": "delta",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "from": "{{cp1}}",
        "to": "{{cp2}}",
        "output": "{{work}}/change.stowdelta"
      },
      "alsoWritten": "change.stowdelta",
      "expect": {
        "version": {
          "equals": 1
        },
        "base_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp1}}"
        },
        "target_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp2}}"
        },
        "document": {
          "equals": "{{work}}/change.stowdelta"
        },
        "sha256": {
          "matches": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
        },
        "files": {
          "equals": 1
        },
        "bytes": {
          "equals": 20
        }
      },
      "returns": "stdout",
      "documentFields": {
        "base_id": "{{cp1}}",
        "target_id": "{{cp2}}"
      },
      "capture": {
        "sha": "sha256"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "apply rebuilds the base plus the delta into a new checkpoint",
      "verb": "apply",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "delta": "{{work}}/change.stowdelta",
        "base": "{{cp1}}",
        "expect-sha256": "{{sha}}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "checkpoint_id": {
          "matches": "^cp_[0-9a-f]+$"
        },
        "parent_checkpoint_id": {
          "equals": "{{cp1}}"
        },
        "files": {
          "equals": 3
        },
        "bytes": {
          "equals": 30
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "applying a delta to a base it was not measured from is refused",
      "verb": "apply",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "delta": "{{work}}/change.stowdelta",
        "base": "{{cp2}}"
      },
      "fail": {
        "contains": "diverged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a delta whose payload no longer matches its digest is refused",
      "verb": "apply",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "delta": "{{work}}/tampered.stowdelta",
        "base": "{{cp1}}"
      },
      "tamper": "change.stowdelta",
      "fail": {
        "contains": "disagrees with"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a substituted destination applies when the receiver is not told the digest, which is why the check is opt-in",
      "verb": "apply",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "delta": "{{work}}/renamed.stowdelta",
        "base": "{{cp1}}"
      },
      "renameInTransit": {
        "from": "{{work}}/change.stowdelta",
        "path": "notes.txt",
        "to": "planted.sh"
      },
      "expect": {
        "files": {
          "equals": 3
        },
        "bytes": {
          "equals": 30
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a delta whose destination was renamed in transit is refused on the document digest",
      "verb": "apply",
      "registry": "a",
      "team": "platform",
      "args": {
        "delta": "{{work}}/renamed.stowdelta",
        "base": "{{cp1}}",
        "expect-sha256": "{{sha}}"
      },
      "renameInTransit": {
        "from": "{{work}}/change.stowdelta",
        "path": "notes.txt",
        "to": "planted.sh"
      },
      "fail": {
        "contains": "does not match the digest"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "collect sweeps the registry it is pointed at and reports what it swept",
      "verb": "collect",
      "expect": {
        "results": {
          "minLength": 2
        }
      },
      "args": {
        "registry-dir": "{{registryA}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "destroy removes the workspace stow created, and says so",
      "verb": "destroy",
      "args": {
        "id": "{{ws}}",
        "registry-dir": "{{registryA}}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "destroyed": {
          "equals": true
        },
        "workspace_id": {
          "equals": "{{ws}}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
